      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The base material can be an equiatomic or near-equiatomic alloy in which Ti and Ni are the primary components and additional elements satisfy the five-element HEA definition.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The proposed intervention is applicable in either an as-cast or thermally homogenized condition.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The relevant operating range is 1000–1400 °C.",
      "field": "conditions; boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "An inert or controlled-oxidation environment will isolate the alloy's mechanical response from oxidation effects.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition will enhance solid-solution strengthening in the Ti-Ni-primary alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo addition may form fine, thermally stable precipitates in the Ti-Ni-primary alloy.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8074761::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo acts as a beta stabilizer in titanium alloys.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo-induced precipitates will refine the microstructure and improve grain-boundary cohesion.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo's high melting point favors elevated-temperature strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Mo interacts strongly with both Ti and Ni in a manner that promotes solid-solution strengthening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Beneficial secondary phases produced by the intervention will hinder dislocation motion.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC8074761::web::000::abstract"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-added alloy will have higher elevated-temperature yield strength than the Mo-free baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7514121::web::020::5_conclusions"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "The Mo-added alloy will have better creep resistance than the Mo-free baseline.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome; mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
